cept2xpm
========


==Abstract==
cept2xpm is a simple tool to convert xpm bitmaps to Cept mosaic graphics.
So you can create graphics using a sophisticated graphic editing tool and
than you can convert them to a BTX compliant format without hassle.


==XPM Format==
The great advantage of the xpm format is, that it is not a binary format 
and it is very easy to parse with a program. That is the reason why i 
choosed this format.

Unfortunately there exist some different types of the format. The converter
accepts only monochrome images. The width must be a mulitple of 2 and the
height must be a multiple of 3. That is because the mosaic graphics on an
cept-videotex screen have a size of 2x3 and the image must fit in that grid.

However, if you take a look with a texteditor to your xpm-file you should
see something like this. If the program does not work you should alter
the file to the format shown below.

/* XPM */
static char * test_xpm[] = {
"60 60 2 1",
" 	c #FFFFFF",
